# --- non-dataset material inside data/ ---
# NOTE: every line here is a regex, comments included. Avoid parentheses and
# other metacharacters or R CMD build fails with "invalid regular expression".
# R treats everything in data/ as packaged datasets and rejects anything that is
# not one. These four are working material: a README, the Census NP2023
# projection inputs, a FREIDA extract, and a rendered table. They stay on disk
# because generators read them from the source tree, but must not enter the build.
^data/README\.md$
^data/census$
^data/freida$
^data/table1_urps_characteristics_2026-07-23\.docx$
# --- data/ is repository material, not package data ---
# Classified all 96 CSVs by who reads them. Exactly ONE is read by package code:
# departure_anchor.csv, inside wc_load_cohort. That function cannot run from an
# installed package regardless, because its primary input WC_COHORT_CSV resolves
# into the isochrones monorepo. Everything else is read by manuscript/, scripts/,
# code/, the Shiny apps or tests, none of which is installed. So nothing here is
# needed by the installed package at runtime.
# Excluding the directory also stops R parsing every CSV as a packaged dataset,
# which five of them fail: three hard errors and two EOF-within-quoted-string.
# The files stay on disk and all 128 in-repo references keep working; the tests
# that read them skip under check via skip_if_no_repo.
# Guarded by tests/testthat/test-package-runtime-inputs.R.
^data$
^docs_site$
